cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "farhand: chat-driven orchestration of a shared computational-chemistry workstation"
abstract: >-
  Submit, monitor, arbitrate and post-process computational chemistry jobs on a
  single shared workstation from a chat client, with no shell access to the
  machine. This release provides two components: a lease-based resource
  arbiter that lets engines with disjoint resource requirements run
  concurrently on one machine, and a job runner that pins each calculation to a
  CPU set, captures its output, and judges success by a per-engine rule rather
  than by exit code alone.
type: software
